Use the physical Python executable identified in `preparation-tool-files.json`; the observed Windows app launcher alias is not byte-readable. Preparation and eventual native launch use the same actual interpreter/environment. Only tool/native identity digests may be saved; no environment values, .env or credentials. Hash Git/Docker file bytes without invoking Docker. Exact native run-campaign command rendering must pin the prepared policy; rendering is not execution. No new paid execution wrapper is in this driver scope.

## Review output

Read the frozen script once in bounded chunks and inspect only necessary native source callpaths for concrete side-effect/identity risks. Verify report claims against code. Write `campaign-preparation-driver/independent-review.md` with separate spec and quality verdicts, exact script/report hashes, findings with file:line and the clear execution boundary: approval permits principal actual preparation only, never a paid run. Do not run source imports, script, probes, native readers, Git/Docker commands, provider calls or tests. A complete actual prepared package still needs its own independent artifact/launch review and the separate fresh user paid grant.
